@startuml
title Stage 0.5 - Design Constraints / Guardrails (Notes)

skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "Stage 0 / 0.5 Guardrails" {
  note as N1
  1) Store owns memory. Nodes hold handles/pointers only.
  2) Queue contains pointers only. Overflow uses DropOldestItem.
  3) OutputNode is the release chain terminator:
     object -> buffer -> frame.
  4) Stage 0.5 adds observability and global meta only.
  5) Stage 1 starts when real RTSP ingest is connected to the pipeline input.
  end note

  note as N2
  Naming/Comments policy:
  - Avoid abbreviations for domain concepts.
  - Write excessive comments.
  - Assume "one month later, I am a different person".
  end note

  note as N3
  Meta store policy:
  - read(): find-only, no create (avoid hallucinated state).
  - write(): create allowed.
  - Callbacks under lock in Stage 0.5:
    callbacks must be short; avoid store re-entry.
  end note
}

@enduml
